{
  "dom_id": "step-q337167",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $\u03a6(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X\u223cN(3,{6}^{2}),$ compute $P(X<13.5).$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.6\\,$ | $\\,0.9505\\,$ | $\\,0.9515\\,$ | $\\,0.9525\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.7\\,$ | $\\,0.9599\\,$ | $\\,0.9608\\,$ | $\\,0.9616\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.8\\,$ | $\\,0.9678\\,$ | $\\,0.9686\\,$ | $\\,0.9693\\,$ |\n\n$P(X<13.5)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Given a normal random variable $X\u223cN(\\mu ,{\\sigma }^{2}),$ we have\n\n$$\nP(X<x)=P(Z<\\frac{x-\\mu }{\\sigma })\n$$\n\nwhere $Z\u223cN(0,1)$ is a standard normal random variable. In our case, we have $\\mu =3$ and $\\sigma =6.$\n\nFirst, we transform $X$ into a standard normal random variable $Z$ by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<13.5) & =P(Z<\\frac{13.5-3}{6}) \\\\  & =P(Z<1.75) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 1.75) \\\\  & =\u03a6(1.75)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070250/assets/e024a5ac6bdd86c88c6ed6cbe3a647281c63e6934c3830288fa01c1d51997e4a.png)\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\n\u03a6(1.75)=0.9599.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(X<13.5)=0.9599.\n$$",
